er crisis  because a lot of people as we're  struggling to get people to get back to  work  now we're going to have even a greater  crisis when people who do not want to  take the vaccine for medical reasons  aren't going to be returning to work and  this is going to be acutely a problem in  hospitals where we have seen hundreds  and hundreds of people who work in  hospitals protesting in my region  because of the vaccine mandate  and those who have already had the virus  and many other reasons that justify not  necessarily having to take the vaccine  but they're not prohibited from going to  work so we're going to see another  downturn in the economy potentially  congressman let's switch gears as we  reflect on the 20th anniversary of 911  what do you remember from that day  you know this is hard to believe it's 20  years uh but it's really a sad day and i  i always remember just uh  you know my son was only 10 years old  i remember actually the weirdest thing  is i was normally would be at work but i  had a dentist appointment  and i happened to be home just waiting  it out and i saw on the news that a  tower hit a plane and hit one of the  towers and everyone said oh a small  plane has crashed into the world trade  center and then it evolved into you know  just a diabolic horror that we all sat  and watched i actually went to the  dentist office and we were hubbled  around a very small tv that they had in  the back room i remember this is 20  years ago that what the technology that  the nice tvs we have today weren't  something you'd see in an office and i  would just remember all of us watching  in horror  um as it unfolded and the second plane  hit and the towers came down and you  know i still just remember just just the  [ __ ] of people running from 911 site  and also one of my  childhood friends was on the plane that  crashed in shanksville pennsylvania  particularly  difficult for our families  and before we let you go your son is a  united states marine we certainly thank  him for his service and he was deployed  to iraq to to fight this war on terror  and as you've seen how it's come to an  end uh and we are at the 20-year  anniversary mark tomorrow of the 9 11  attacks have you spoken to him about his  reflections  yeah he's actually just had his last  active duty day last week on the marine  corps i have to tell you something very  funny i i said to him i said geez i  think this is i feel sort of relieved  that  that you're moving to uh the reserve  ranks and you said you know this is one  of the reasons i would consider staying  in is because we need people to protect  america and keep us safe we need good  people serving our military and i was  just uh i was surprised to hear that but  uh  i'm grateful that he is uh you know a  person who cares deeply about our  country and his answer  uh to service was uh was for real and i  know there are there he's just one of of  millions who have answered the call to  serve the people who give ultimately end  up giving so much in the end and want to  give more and that's the hallmark of  those brave and honorable folks like  your son congresswoman claudia tenney  thank you very much thank  thank you so much hi everyone i'm brian  kilmeade i want you to do me a favor i  want you to click to subscribe to the  fox news youtube page this is the only  way that i know for sure that you're not  going to miss any great commentary any  great news bites any great interviews  coming your way on fox you can get it  all here on youtube so subscribe right  now

